WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.720
Testing an ethical framework requires
high-pressure scenarios that force our

2
00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:06.940
moral intuitions to the breaking point.

3
00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:11.200
Look at the left side. In Singer's shallow
pond, if you see a toddler

4
00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:14.580
drowning, you save them despite ruining
expensive shoes.

5
00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:17.840
The personal cost is minor. The benefit is
a life.

6
00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:21.720
Now, the right panel. Thomson poses a
different scenario.

7
00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:25.360
You wake up medically connected to an
unconscious violinist.

8
00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:28.700
Unplugging reclaims physical autonomy, but
ends his life.

9
00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:33.060
the variables pit bodily freedom against
preserving another person.

10
00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.320
Where do these two scenarios align and
diverge?

11
00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:40.960
Finding where an analogy fails clarifies
our core priorities and provides a

12
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.500
concrete starting point for rigorous
analysis.
